{
 "definitions": {
  "TRC": "Tax Return Code - a Thomson Reuters-defined (system-assigned, required) code of form NN-NNN that ties a trial-balance/general-ledger account to a specific line of the tax return. Ranges: 10-/11- assets, 20-/21-/22- liabilities & equity, 30-/31- page 1 income (and Sch K income), 40- COGS (Form 1125-A), 41- page 1 deductions, 60- Schedule M-1, 62- Schedule M-2. NOT 'Tax Reconciliation Code'.",
  "TCC": "Tax Combination Code - an optional, user-defined code of up to 3 characters used together with a TRC to subdivide/group accounts within one return line (e.g., itemizing the line 26 Other Deductions statement or Sch L 'other' statements) and control white-paper/statement detail; required for cross-tie printing on 1120 consolidated returns. Descriptions maintained via the TCC/PC/MCC Descriptions menu. NOT 'Tax Code Category'.",
  "MRC": "(related) M-3 Return Code - assigns Schedule M-3 line items (I-, E- series); only allowed on accounts with 30-/40-range TRCs."
 },
