 "confidence_notes": "Definitions of TRC (Tax Return Code) and TCC (Tax Combination Code) are verified from multiple Thomson Reuters/RIA (GoSystem) guides. Code values marked verified:true were confirmed from search-engine excerpts of the official GoSystem TRC/MRC PDFs on riahelp.com (RIA = Thomson Reuters, GoSystem's publisher) and TR help pages; the PDFs themselves could NOT be downloaded in this sandbox (thomsonreuters.com and riahelp.com blocked by network policy), so values were not read from the full tables. Notes say when a code was seen on a sibling-form sheet (1120-C/1120S/1120-F/1120-RIC/1120-REIT/1120-PC) rather than the plain 1120 sheet; the TRC numbering is shared across the 1120 family (TRC_All.pdf), so these are high but not certain confidence. Line numbers are mapped to the current Form 1120 layout by the researcher; some sheet line numbers were from older/sibling forms. verified:false = inferred codes or illustrative user-defined TCCs. Form 1120 line 26 detail (utilities, professional fees, office) has no confirmed dedicated TRCs: the GoSystem convention is TRC 41-900 subdivided by firm-defined TCCs. TCC values are user-defined, so there is no canonical TCC list. Workpapers CS/Accounting CS/UltraTax use a different numeric scheme (e.g., 100 gross receipts, 101 returns & allowances) - do not mix. Before production use, download 1120_TRC_MRC.pdf for the target tax year to confirm.",
